    "final_answer": "Based on my thorough research of ESPN's NBA coverage, here is my final answer:\n\n## NBA Trade Updates from ESPN (Past 2 Days)\n\n**Finding: No new NBA trades have occurred within the past 2 days (October 1-3, 2026).**\n\nESPN's NBA trade tracker, most recently updated on September 22, 2026, shows that the most recent trade activity was on that date. The NBA is currently in preseason mode (training camps have begun), and the offseason trade window has effectively closed.\n\n### Most Recent NBA Trade on ESPN:\n**September 22, 2026 - Atlanta Hawks / Charlotte Hornets**\n- **Charlotte Hornets received:** Buddy Hield (G), Ryan Nembhard (G), and cash considerations\n- **Atlanta Hawks received:** Dorian Finney-Smith (F)\n\n### Recent NBA News in the Past 2 Days (Not Trades, but Related):\n- Veteran PG D'Angelo Russell was waived by the Memphis Grizzlies and hit free agency\n- Hornets star Kon Knueppel sidelined with hamstring injury\n- Curry reached a 2-year, $116 million extension with the Warriors (Sept. 25)\n- Various injury updates and NBA Rank/analysis articles (Brunson wrist surgery, Flagg's rookie debut card, NBA Rank audit, etc.)\n\n### Summary:\nWithin the past 2 days (Oct 1-3, 2026), ESPN has reported **no actual NBA trades**. The latest player movement reported was a waiver (Russell waived by Grizzlies), and most of the recent news has centered on contract extensions, injury updates, and season previews. The Hawks-Hornets swap involving Dorian Finney-Smith on September 22 remains the most recent actual trade listed on ESPN's 2026 offseason trade tracker.",
